\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Steady Vs Dlr Early; Seen Depreciating \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1999\par 09:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Thursday, but dealers predict it will depreciate by the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  At about 0747 GMT, the dollar was between ROL14,950 and ROL15,000, little changed from late Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the leu is likely to depreciate slightly by the end of the session amid falling money market rates. The overnight money market rate was quoted between 20% and 80%, down from 40% and 100% Wednesday, while the rate for one-week deposits was quoted between 50% and 100%, from 50% and 115% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday to halt the leu's rapid fall. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold "only a few million dollars" when the dollar was trading at more than ROL15,000, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market observers predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will look to keep tight control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the government negotiates a new stand-by loan from the International Monetary Fund. Talks are expected to conclude by April 22. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0749GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4f02t6v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
