\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Dn Vs Dlr In Thin Trade; Seen Falling Further \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Wednesday with dealers predicting that the unit will continue to fall over the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0745 GMT, the dollar was between ROL15,350 and ROL15,650, up from ROL15,250 and ROL15,300 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu depreciated in early trading amid increasing dollar demand from banks. "There is high leu liquidity which makes banks want to buy dollars," a dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the market remains calm in thin early trading. \par \par \uc2  The high leu liquidity has also pushed down money market rates. The overnight money market rate was quoted early Wednesday at between 50% and 100%, from between 100% and 180% Tuesday. The leu one week deposit rate was between 100% and 220%, down from 140% and 250% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market Wednesday by attracting leu deposits at high rates to slow the unit's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, the leu has depreciated 28.9%, compared with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official target of 40% depreciation for the whole of 1999. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 31-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0754GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3v02i9e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\