\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Steady Vs Dlr In Thin Early Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is seen steady against the dollar in thin but tense trade early Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0825 GMT, the dollar was between ROL15,500 and ROL16,800, little changed from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was thin amid uncertainty over the future direction of the leu. A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu could continue to depreciate, although participants fear there could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The leu dropped 1.4% against the dollar Thursday, with the market being hit by dollar sales at midday by profit-takers, which pushed the dollar down to between ROL12,000 and ROL14,500. But the leu resumed its depreciation trend later to close around ROL16,000 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, the leu has depreciated 28.2%, compared with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official target of 40% depreciation for the whole of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate was quoted Friday at between 50% and 100%, while the rates for one-week deposits were between 70% and 170%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quoted its reference rate Wednesday at ROL15,115. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu predicted Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will return to calm and that the leu could appreciate. \par \par \uc2  Isarescu said the leu's depreciation in the past few days reflected the country's ailing economy. He said the fall has been exacerbated by rating agencies downgrading Romania's credit ratings, and by rumors in the media about the country possibly defaulting on foreign debts. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0859GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3j027jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
