\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  C.Bank vows to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to boost  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Popeski \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, March 18 (Reuters) - The governor of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) pledged on Thursday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever required to support the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its sharp plunge this week on volatile markets. \par \par \uc2  "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when and where it is needed," Mugur Isarescu told parliament's upper house, the Senate, a day after the leu sank more than five percent against the dollar, its largest single-day decline this year. \par \par \uc2  "The situation reflects tension accumulated within the economy and in public life. At the moment, there is a big psychological component reflected by big spreads on markets." \par \par \uc2  The leu started the day by initially resuming its fall from Wednesday's close of 15,500/17,000 and then regained some of the lost ground. At mid-day, it was swinging wildly from quotes of 11,000 to 16,000/18,000 and by mid-afternoon, quotes were standing at 15,000/17,000. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said the BNR was trying to sell some treasury notes from its portfolio but no deals appear to have been done. There was no apparent direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helped by dollar selling orders from corporate clients at mid-day. Orders were relatively moderate, but in the tumult even small amounts were prompting big swings. \par \par \uc2  The centrist coalition government cut its weekly meeting to 90 minutes and put off a discussion on a privatisation bill. Leaders of the four coalition parties agreed to meet next week to discuss the outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Traian Remes told reporters a promised plan to redress the leu's situation would be ready next week. He said he had "no moral right" to disclose details as this could affect markets at a "critical" point for the leu. \par \par \uc2  Isarescu said the bank had taken no action during Wednesday's big drop. The Finance Ministry, he said, had had to honour redemption of $60 million in domestic bonds. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now working with a projected leu depreciation of about 40 percent, compared to 31-32 percent as set down in the 1999 budget. Markets would quickly calm down and the depreciation would be more gradual from next month. \par \par \uc2  The leu, which started the New Year at about 11,000 to the dollar, has been battered by poor economic performance and large trade deficits. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials say a correction is required as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appreciated in real terms in the past two years due to high capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have expressed concern about Romania's ability to meet servicing of more than $2 billion in public debt, with a peak in May and June. The government is negotiating a new loan arrangement with the World Bank, a pre-requisite for further credits from the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  On Bucharest streets, the leu rebounded slightly at exchange offices from Wednesday's selling quotes of up to 23,000. \par \par \uc2  Passersby gaped at rates posted on billboards and calculated out loud the prices of imported goods. Dozens of shops selling appliances shut their doors and declared a day of stock-taking. \par \par \uc2  "How much do you think they will push up the price of a mobile phone?" one young man asked a friend. \par \par \uc2  Small queues formed outside banks of depositors trying to change leu deposits into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Former Prime Minister Petre Roman, now Senate Chairman and leader of the Social Democrats, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculation. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmly to stem spculation and stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Roman told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Isarescu said the bank's strategy called for a faster depreciation in the first months of the year and a more gradual decline from April. \par \par \uc2  After closing on Wednesday at 15,500/700, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was traded in volatile conditions through the morning. \par \par \uc2  The leu initially resumed its fall and then regained some of the lost ground. By mid-day, quotes ranged from 16,000/18,000 to 14,000/17,000 and most dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken no action on the market. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helped by some dollar selling orders from corporate clients at mid-day. Orders were relatively moderate, but in the tumult even small amounts were prompting big swings. \par \par \uc2  The leu started the week at 13,850 to the dollar. At the New Year, it was trading at about 11,000. \par \par \uc2  ((Bucharest Newsroom +40 1 312-0264 fax +40 1 315-8448 e-mail bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3i03er9\