\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Wednesday, with dealers saying it might extend its slide over the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0805 GMT, the dollar was between ROL14,350 and ROL14,750, up from ROL14,200 and ROL14,600 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The leu fell sharply in hectic trade Tuesday despite the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market, where it attracted leu deposits at very high rates in a bid to divert banks from investing in dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quoted its reference rate Tuesday at ROL14,040 per dollar, up 2.5% from Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar demand continued despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some dealers said that only money market rates at around 400% could halt the leu's fall. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate was quoted early Wednesday at between 160% and 280%, while the rate for one-week deposits was around 200%. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was much calmer early Wednesday but predicted the leu's fast depreciation might resume at some point in the day if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market. \par \par \uc2  There was no comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the leu's fall. \par \par \uc2  Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said that the "nervous depreciation" of the leu will halt around the end of March and will be followed by a "gradual depreciation" in April. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees a 40% depreciation of the leu this year, based on 32% annual inflation. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0835GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3h023id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
