\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu's Sharp Depreciation Spreads Panic \b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 19:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The depreciation of the Romanian leu has become critical after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply again Wednesday, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  The leu dropped 5.8% against the dollar in hectic trade Wednesday after a 2.5% fall Tuesday. So far this year, the leu has depreciated 27,2%, clearly overshooting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official target of 40% depreciation in 1999. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody is desperate to buy dollars, at any price," a dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said. "Somebody must do something to halt the trend, if it can or if it has the interest to do it," he said, referring to a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the fast depreciation trend could be stopped only by a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They said the longer the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is delayed, the higher the costs in terms of the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is a moment of panic," said a top official at a foreign bank in Romania, adding that the leu's depreciation has been caused by speculative trading. "The next two weeks will be crucial in proving whether the Romanian market is mature enough to return to normal," he said. \par \par \uc2  The leu's depreciation Wednesday also sparked panic among ordinary Romanians, who rushed to exchange savings in lei for dollars. In Bucharest, the exchanged houses bought the dollar at ROL16,000 and sold it at more than ROL18,000. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar closed at between ROL15,500 and ROL18,000, up from ROL14,400 and ROL14,500 early Wednesday and ROL14,200 and ROL14,600 late Tuesday. The National Bank of Romania quoted its reference rate at ROL14,900, from ROL14,040 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The leu's depreciation initially was seen as a positive sign by analysts. A weaker leu was expected to help the government narrow its current account deficit, which was estimated at $2.3 billion in 1998. Adding the $2.2 billion in foreign debts that must be repaid this year, it become clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to choose between meeting payments and supporting the leu. \par \par \uc2  But the leu fall in the past days boosted concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to halt the leu from disaster. \par \par \uc2  The official at the foreign bank said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and calm the market by attracting leu deposits on money market and diverting banks from investing in dollars. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, however, is unlikely as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - quoted at $1.59 billion at the end of February - to pay back foreign debts. \par \par \uc2  But if the leu continues to fall, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  via administrative measures, such as implementing the crawling peg, the official said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Adrian Vasilescu said in a radio interview Wednesday that the leu's depreciation trend won't continue in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzen (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-03-99 \par \par \uc2  1825GMT \par \par \uc2  1196 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3h020yn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
