\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Stronger Vs Dlr Early Amid High Money Mkt Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly stronger against the dollar early Friday, with dealers predicting the leu might appreciate in the day amid high money market rates. \par \par \uc2  At about 0858 GMT, the dollar was between ROL13,540 and ROL13,580, down from ROL13,550 and ROL13,600 from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu rallied against the dollar in early trading as the money market rates rose, with the overnight rate quoted at between 150% and 200%, up from less of 100% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The increase in money market rates was determined by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday when it attracted leu deposits at high rates to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid depreciation, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said earlier this week that the "nervous depreciation" of the leu will halt around the end of March and will be followed by a "gradual depreciation" in April. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees a 40% depreciation of the leu this year, based on 32% annual inflation. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197 ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0859GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3c01zu7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
