\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Closes Sharply Dn; Seen Falling 1.5% Tue \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 19:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu closed sharply lower Tuesday, after resuming its fast depreciation trend in hectic trade after the fall in overnight money market rates, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They added that only a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days would halt its fast fall. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed the session at between ROL13,400 and ROL13,450, up from between ROL13,000 and ROL13,100 at the opening. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reference rate rose to ROL13,320, up 1.5% from Monday \par \par \uc2  The leu's decline followed the fall in money market rates on increasing leu liquidity. The overnight money market rate dropped to around 60% Tuesday from more than 400% Monday. \par \par \uc2  The leu halted its depreciation Friday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attracted leu deposits at high rates to divert banks' attention from investing in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the up-and-downs of Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market rates would have a positive effect by hurting speculative trading. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators won't be able to predict any (future) evolution of the market," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Adrian Vasilescu told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Vasilescu predicted the "nervous depreciation" of the leu will end around end March and will be followed by a "gradual depreciation" in April. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees a 40% depreciation of the leu this year, on 32% annual inflation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the target isn't realistic as the leu already depreciated by around 15% this year. \par \par \uc2  To control the leu, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to choose between selling dollars on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keeping money market rates. \par \par \uc2  But selling dollars will mean hurting the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves that are badly needed for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt payments, while high money market rates will make more expensive the financing of the budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold ROL1.3 trillion in three-month Treasury bills at an average yield of 84.95%, up from 67.39% in the previous auction last week. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-03-99 \par \par \uc2  1802GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3901uuh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
