\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Depreciation Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Tuesday and is seen depreciating further amid low money market rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0815 GMT, the dollar was trading at between ROL12,890 and ROL12,930, up from between ROL12,810 and ROL12,840 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu resumed its depreciation trend in early trading as money market rates dropped sharply. The overnight money market was quoted at about 5% Tuesday, from 40% Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the banks will begin investing in dollars unless the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the leu. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly Friday, when it sold about $35 million to calm the fast depreciation of the leu, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the first two months of this year, the leu has depreciated by 14.27% against the dollar, making it unlikely for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reach its target of 35% annual depreciation of the leu in 1999. \par \par \uc2  With prospects for a new stand-by agreement with the International Monetary Fund in June, some dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should meantime encourage a weaker leu in order to narrow the current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-03-99 \par \par 