\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1999\par 09:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Tuesday, with dealers predicting a further fall amid speculative moves by banks. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL12,510 and ROL12,545, up from between ROL12,435 and ROL12,465 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu depreciated in early trading on dollar demand from banks. "The leu is going lower on speculative moves," the dealer said. He said the banks are investing in dollars with the intention of selling them later to take profits on the leu's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu will continue to depreciate unless the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could either sell dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or attract leu deposits at high rates to divert banks from investing in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate remained at 75% Tuesday, unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market participants are also worried by media reports announcing the resignation of the management of the country's largest state bank, the Romanian Bank for Foreign Trade, or Bancorex. \par \par \uc2  "When there is something unclear about Bancorex, people are worried," a dealer said. He said the lack of official news on the bank's restructuring also contributed to investors' concerns. \par \par \uc2  Media reports late Monday said Chairman Vlad Soare, together with the bank's management team, had to resign after failing to present a feasible plan for the bank's restructuring. The reform of Bancorex is one of the conditions imposed by the International Monetary Fund for signing a new financial agreement with the government. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0817GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2n01gnm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
