\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1999\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets at mid-day on Thursday to ease pressure on the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the unit weakened towards 12,300 to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR drained leu funds at about 140-150 percent and showed up afterwards on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  side selling dollars," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed to about 12,200/230 against 12,280/300 in early trading when it faced increased pressure due to declining money market rates and speculative deals ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  Short-term money market prices soared to about 130/200 percent from around 75/100 percent at the opening. Some dealers said the BNR may have spent up to $15 million in Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier in the week, the BNR acted on both markets to cap a faster downswing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Local media reports on Thursday quoted Finance Ministry sources as saying a visiting International Monetary Fund team believed the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was depreciating too quickly. \par \par \uc2  IMF officials in Bucharest were not immediately available to comment. \par \par \uc2  The leu traded near 11,000 to the dollar in the New Year. Monthly inflation quickened to three percent in January from 2.2 percent in December 1998. ((Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2b04tpr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
