\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1999\par 14:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The faster peace of depreciation in recent weeks seems to confirm analysts and dealers' expectations. The leu fell by almost 5% last week, after it slipped 6% in January. So far in 1999 the leu has depreciated by 9.6%, compared with 45.9% in 1998. The government expects 1999 inflation to fall to 25% from 40.6% last year. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, at 1330GMT, the dollar was traded at between ROL12,130 and ROL12,170, up from between ROL12,060 and ROL12,080 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Romania, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , isn't trying to stop the leu's fall although it is trying to slow the rate of decline. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as many times as it needs to calm down the market," said Mugur Stet, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman. "But the exchange rate will be decided only by the market," he said, adding that the recent pressure on the leu was caused by the speculative trading by commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can still be a force in the market. Even if it chooses to preserve its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves which stood at $1.98 billion at the end of January, the bank can act through the money market by attracting leu deposits at very high rates, which make investments in lei more profitable than those in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, monetary policy is unlikely to have any success over the longer term if it is not backed by a comprehensive program of structural reforms, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The recent completion of a number of privatizations and and its latest budget plans indicate the government is taking market reforms more seriously. \par \par \uc2  The loss-making oil refinery Petromidia was sold to Turkey's Akmaya, while France's Renault SA is negotiating for the takeover of automaker Automobile Dacia. \par \par \uc2  The government has begun the legal process leading to a declaration of bankruptcy for a further 49 state-owned companies that operate at a loss. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-02-99 \par \par \uc2  1334GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2a0138q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
