\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Stronger Vs Dlr Early On High Money Mkt Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1999\par 09:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is stronger against the dollar early Wednesday on dollar sales by banks that want to invest in leu deposits. \par \par \uc2  At 0805 GMT, the dollar was trading at between ROL12,060 and ROL12,080, down from ROL12,080 and ROL12,100 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The leu's rally against the dollar in the past two days followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday on both \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets that stemmed the leu's fast fall. \par \par \uc2  On the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attracted leu deposits at high rates, making investments in leu more profitable than those in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate remained at around 150% Wednesday, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said that taking into account the high money market rates, banks would prefer to sell dollars to make leu deposits. But he predicted the leu's fall might resume in the coming days as interest rates are expected to fall at the end of the week. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0826GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2a012uh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
