\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Stronger Vs Dlr Early; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1999\par 09:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is stronger against the dollar early Tuesday following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday that stopped the leu's fast fall. \par \par \uc2  At 0820 GMT, the dollar was trading at between ROL12,120 and ROL12,155, down from ROL12,180 and ROL12,220 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. On the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attracted leu deposits at high rates, making the investments in leu more profitable than those in dollars. On the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold small amounts of dollars to slow the leu's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate rose to around 150% Tuesday from 130% Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said the pressure on the leu has decreased early Tuesday, for the first time in the past 10 days since the leu depreciated by more than 4%. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $15 million to stop the leu's slide against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu depreciation might resume in the coming days but at a slower speed. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is deliberately letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciate to stimulate exports and thus narrow the rising trade deficit. The trade deficit in the 11 months to November rose to $3.06 billion from $2.29 billion in the same period a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0842GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv29012ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
