\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop up the leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1999\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold dollars on the interbank market on Monday to temper continuous pressure on the local leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the BNR had entered the market when the leu traded near 12,220/280 to the dollar, helping it to firm towards bid quotes of 12,185. The BNR had previously drained money market funds to help the unit recover from lows of 12,280/310. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the BNR may have spent up to $10 million in Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The extent of drainage on the money market was unknown. \par \par \uc2  "The market has calmed down for a while but pressure on the leu remains," said one trader. "There are some big players chasing leu funds but also willing to switch to the dollar. There might be clients' notes behind that pressure as well." \par \par \uc2  The leu was trading at mid-afternoon near 12,220/270 while short-term money market prices swelled to about 150/300 percent from 80/110 at the opening, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Operators saw the leu closing Monday near 12,220/260 and said it was likely to decline further in the coming days unless the BNR offered the unit further support. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the BNR made repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both money and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to contain a faster downswing of the leu. BNR officials have pledged to step into the market whenever pressure needs to be offset. ((Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2804ucf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
