\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Romania - Feb 4. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1999\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Following are highlights of the main stories in Romanian newspapers on Thursday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  All the papers report on Romania's President Emil Constantinescu's plans to upgrade the country's transport, communications and enrgy sectors. \par \par \uc2  ECONOMIC \par \par \uc2  ZIARUL FINANCIAR \par \par \uc2  - Romania's main privatisation agency, the State Ownership Fund (FPS), privatised 159 companies in which it had majority stakes last January, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, selling around $15 million on the local interbank market to temper the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  - Austrian brewer Brau Union AG holds 21 percent of the Romanian beer market, with an output of around two million hectoliters, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  BURSA \par \par \uc2  - Around 70 percent of 1999 state budget revenues will come from taxes imposed on individuals, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  ADEVARUL \par \par \uc2  - Transport Minister Traian Basescu proposed that the debts of the former railway authority SNCFR be transfered to the public debt, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  - A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is not a solution for Romania, the papaer says in an editorial. \par \par \uc2  ROMANIA LIBERA \par \par \uc2  - Steel mill Sidex exported in January 127,400 tonnes cashing in around $28 million, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  - The BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $1.98 billion at end-January, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  EVENIMENTUL ZILEI \par \par \uc2  - Black Sea-based refinery Petromidia will receive over the next two weeks its first crude shipments from the Caspian region, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  GENERAL \par \par \uc2  ZIARUL FINANCIAR \par \par \uc2  - The number of influenza cases rose to 9,092 last week, four times higher from the previous week, but no deaths were reported, the paper says. \par \par \uc2  EVENIMENTUL ZILEI \par \par \uc2  - The U.S. heavy metal group Metallica might perform in Bucharest on June, the paper says. ($=11,948 lei) ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)) REUTERS. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv24055ws\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
