\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Dn Vs Dlr Early; Ctrl Bk Action Slows Downtrend \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1999\par 09:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Thursday but the speed of its depreciation is slower than in the previous days following the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0820 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL12,080 and ROL12,110, up from ROL12,040 and ROL12,060 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu is expected to continue its depreciation over the day, but with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintaining tight control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate of decline. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, selling about $15 million, to slow the leu's fast fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market Wednesday, attracting leu deposits at high rates to divert banks from investing in dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday on the money market if the leu resumes its rapid rate of decline. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate rose to around 130% Thursday, from 70% early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The leu has depreciated sharply this week, by more than 3% against the dollar, on heavy dollar demand from banks which were concerned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is deliberately letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciate to stimulate exports and thus narrow the rising trade deficit. \par \par \uc2  The latest statistics showed the trade deficit in the 11 months to November rose to $3.06 billion from $2.29 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  However, traders also said that the leu's rapid depreciation isn't a cause for concern as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enough reserves to control the decline. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0839GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2400uha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
