\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Romania c.bank calms pressure on the leu. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mirela Eremia \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Feb 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) on Wednesday said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local interbank and money markets to brake a decline in the leu and promised a close watch on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's further movements. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the market needs to be calmed down," BNR spokesman Mugur Stet said. \par \par \uc2  He said the BNR's policy would maintain its focus on controlling the money supply and on keeping a market-determined exchange rate as an "element of credibility". \par \par \uc2  Dealers earlier said the BNR had sold dollars and drained money market funds after the unit had slumped to 12,100 to the dollar from Tuesday's close of 12,020/50 amid speculative purchases by banks and increased corporate hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped the leu firm at mid-day to quotes near 11,965/12,040 and propelled money market prices towards 100/140 percent against 70/80 percent at the opening. \par \par \uc2  But the recovery was shortlived. The unit weakened again in afternoon trading to close at 12,040/060. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR moves were more decisive on the money market," said a dealer. "But if you look at the closing prices that's an indication that the market preferred to stay long on dollars." \par \par \uc2  Stet gave no figure on what the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had cost. Some traders estimated it at some $15 million. They also said the bank paid around 130 percent on drainage of one-and two-week funds. \par \par \uc2  Latest data put the BNR's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at $1.97 billion at end-January. \par \par \uc2  Stet noted the BNR had paid earlier this week around $200 million to service debts to the European Union. The amount was a part of February's total payments on the public and public-guaranteed debt of around $388 million. \par \par \uc2  Operators saw the leu likely to stay under pressure on Thursday when position adjustments were likely to continue, probably linked to week-end money deals. They also said short-term rates were expected to remain near current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the leu could finish the week near 12,100/150 despite some support from the money market side," said one dealer, adding that the unit might quote near 12,500 at end-February. \par \par \uc2  The leu has weakened around three percent this week and by more than nine percent since the New Year. \par \par \uc2  The decline came against the background of poor economic indicators, with gross domestic product estimated to have slumped 5.5 percent in 1998 after a 6.6 percent plunge the previous year. Forecasts have it contracting this year too. \par \par \uc2  Data issued on Monday also showed the 11-month trade balance in FOB prices showed a deficit of $2.24 billion against around $1.6 billion in the same 1997 period. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the indicators had no direct impact on trading. \par \par \uc2  "The poor results have been priced in by the market even before they were issued," said one. "And the leu decline in the recent period had only confirmed that pessimism." \par \par \uc2  Overnight and one-week prices rose to 100/140 percent after the BNR actions, against 70/85 percent in early trading. \par \par \uc2  BNR officials were not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said increased pressure on the leu had come from speculative position adjustments by banks. Some said the BNR had spent about $15 million in Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The leu has depreciated by more than 2.5 percent since end-January due to banks' speculative moves and increased hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand from corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  Some operators said pressure on the leu was likely to continue this month as energy importers were expected to show up on the market. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv23059uf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
