\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 1999\par 09:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Monday on increasing dollar demand, with dealers predicting a further fall for the leu by the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0835 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL11,740 and ROL11,770, up from ROL11,660 and ROL11,690 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu depreciated in early trading on increasing dollar demand from banks. He said that foreign companies repatriating profits and importers' demand have also increased the need for dollars. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers predicted the leu will continue to fall over the week, with little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected from the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might let the leu fall freely until spring, to foster exports. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm the market in the case of a major depreciation of the leu. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate dropped to around 55% Monday, from 85% Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0848GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2100qxr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
