\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Slightly Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1999\par 09:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly lower against the dollar early Wednesday, with dealers predicting a further fall on increasing dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  At 0827 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL11,500 and ROL11,515, up from ROL11,475 and ROL11,500 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu fell against the dollar in early trade on dollar demand from both banks and importers. He said banks seem to be interested in boosting their dollar positions ahead of government's key loan negotiations with the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Talks with the World Bank are expected to start later Wednesday, while negotiations with the IMF might be resumed at the end of January. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar demand was also boosted by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which were quoted at $1.8 billion as of Jan. 13, up from around $1.66 billion at the end of December. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials predicted the leu will depreciate by a maximum 35% this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen attracting leu deposits Tuesday, in a bid to divert banks' attention from investing in dollars. On the money market, leu liquidity is high with the overnight money market rate at around 60%, up from 45% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold ROL1.8 trillion in three-month Treasury bills at an average yield of 71.63%, up from 65.22% in the previous auction last week. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0832GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1k00gwi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
