\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Stronger Vs Dlr; Seen Resuming Depreciation \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 1999\par 09:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is slightly stronger against the dollar early Monday, but dealers predict the leu will resume its depreciation. \par \par \uc2  At 0740 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL11,245 and ROL11,265, down from ROL11,270 and ROL11,290 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu is expected to resume its depreciation, but at a slower rate than last week, when it slid 2.8%. \par \par \uc2  The dealer predicted that the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control the rate of depreciation. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have predicted a maximum 35% depreciation for the leu this year but dealers said the figure is too optimistic if the leu maintains its current falling trend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the money market last week, attracting leu deposits at high rates to drain leu liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money-market rate remained at around 35% Monday, little changed from Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0817GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1b006rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
