\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Steady Vs Dlr Early; Expected To Continue Stable \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1999\par 09:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Friday, with dealers predicting calm trading during the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0815 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL11,255 and ROL11,275, almost unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu is expected to remain steady at the current level Friday as dollar demand is being met by dollar sales from banks that need lei. \par \par \uc2  He said the leu's fall will resume next week, but predicted that the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control the speed of depreciation. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $40 million to slow the leu's slide against the dollar, some dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials predicted the maximum depreciation of the leu in 1999 would be 35%, conditional on an annual inflation rate of 25%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market again Thursday, as it did it every day this week, when it attracted leu deposits at high rates in order to divert banks' attention from investing in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money-market rate rose to around 35% Friday, up from 30% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-99 \par \par \uc2  0838GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokum