\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to temper leu fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1998\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Dec 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both interbank and money markets in mid-day trading on Thursday, selling moderate amounts of dollars to temper the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharp downswing, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the leu weakened to around 10,500/15 to the dollar," said one dealer with a foreign bank. "The increased pressure had come from several banks' weekend money deals and from importers' large dollar purchases." \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said the BNR had drained one-week leu funds from the money market, pushing prices towards 120/150 percent from 80/100 in early trading. They said the move had offered an indirect support to the leu. \par \par \uc2  The unit firmed towards 10,465/80 to the dollar after the BNR moves, but immediatelly fell back to 10,500/30. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not available to comment. \par \par \uc2  The leu opened lower at 10,460/90 against Wednesday's close at around 10,390/420. \par \par \uc2  Short-term money market rates opened slightly up at 90/125 percent from previous close of 80/120 percent. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). REUTERS. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duca02o94\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
