\par\par \b \uc2  Romanian Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Further Fall Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 09:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Wednesday with dealers predicting the falling trend will continue over the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL10,140 and ROL10,170, up from between ROL10,125 and ROL10,1500 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Romania said the pressure on the leu increased in early trading although there was little dollar demand from importers. He said the leu depreciation might be caused by banks that want to accumulate dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell dollars to halt a fast depreciation of the leu. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and selling about $25-$30 million to stop the fast fall of the leu, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate dropped at around 85% early Wednesday, from 100% Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0826GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc201s2k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
