\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Romanian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop leu. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mirela Eremia \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1998\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Nov 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market on Thursday, selling dollars to prop the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since it slipped past 10,000 to the dollar four days ago. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the action, in two waves, could ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days. \par \par \uc2  They said the BNR took action after the leu dived to about 10,193 to the dollar in early trade from about 10,140 at Wednesday's close. The second wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came at midday, hoisting the leu to about 10,060 from 10,143. \par \par \uc2  "We've been waiting for such action through the week since the leu moved into five digits," said one dealer. "The dollar surge was driven by position adjustments and some import bills, but the market calmed down on BNR support for the leu." \par \par \uc2  The leu's passage through the sensitive 10,000 level took place in calm interbank trading. But Romanian consumers, who have seen the leu sink from 21 to the dollar when the communist era ended nine years ago, feared new bouts of inflation. \par \par \uc2  The indicative rate calculated by the BNR firmed to 10,053 from Wednesday's 10,080. But it was down from 9,877 a week ago. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said sliding short-term money market rates might have been behind a faster leu fall in recent days. Rates hovered near 50/80 percent against some 110/120 a week ago. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined comment on Thursday. But BNR officials had been at pains previously to point to a combination of factors behind the leu's decline - a large current account deficit, inflation and poor productivity. \par \par \uc2  The market has been unmoved by the most recent outbreak of Romania's recurrent political infighting, with leftist and nationalist opposition parties boycotting parliamentary debates. \par \par \uc2  The assembly on Thursday postponed a vote on a new BNR board, though parliamentary commissions agreed on its composition, with Mugur Isarescu retaining the post of governor which he has held since 1990. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen continuous political rows this year and the market failed to react," said one. "And as we are keeping nearly the same team at the BNR, I don't see a major worry." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the leu might stay relatively stable for a while but the near-term outlook was fpr a further slide, with interbank prices seen between 10,500 and 10,800 in the new year. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the BNR will allow it to slip below 11,000 this year," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "For a while, the leu might gain some support from an expected pick up in money market rates ahead of the end of this month." \par \par \uc2  The leu opened the year at about 8,000 to the dollar and lost ground gradually over several months. It has sunk more than four percent since October and the BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly early in November to cushion its fall. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubq03m31\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
