\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to prop up leu. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1998\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Nov 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) stepped in for a second wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local interbank market on Thursday, selling dollars to check the slide of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BNR entered the market for the second time today, selling relatively significant amounts of dollars as the leu traded near 10,135/150," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day the BNR acted to stop a leu fall after it weakened to quotes of 10,180/205 to the dollar from 10,170/200 at open and 10,130/150 the previous day. The leu firmed to 10,090/110. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said pressure on the leu came from banks going long on dollars. Some say lower money market rates, at around 50/80 percent compared to 100/115 percent a week ago, might have pushed investors to shift positions. \par \par \uc2  The leu passed the sensitive 10,000 threshold on Monday in a calm interbank market. It then dived to about 10,130/150 in the following days, but the BNR kept out of the market. \par \par \uc2  Operators said BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could help ease pressure on the leu in the coming hours. Some saw the leu stabilising near 10,100/120 at close on Thursday. But most dealers were reluctant to make any prediction for the coming days. ((Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2