\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bank Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  To Slow The Leu's Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 1998\par 12:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of Romania was seen selling dollars in early trading Wednesday in an attempt to slow the leu's (ROL) fast fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the dollar was traded between ROL10,125 and ROL10,140, a dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said. He estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $5 million. \par \par \uc2  At 1030 GMT, the dollar was traded between ROL10,100 and ROL10,110. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the depreciation in early trading was a result of increasing dollar demand from importers' buying orders. \par \par \uc2  The pressure on the leu has decreased in midday trading, but dealers said a depreciation trend will remain for the rest of the session. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was seen trying to attract leu deposits with high money market rates to divert the bank's attention from the dollar, but nothing much has been materialized so far, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1102GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubp01g8x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
