\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to temper leu fall-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1998\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Nov 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) sold small amounts of dollars to calm pressure on the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the unit slumped to about 9,830/900 to the dollar in early trading on Tuesday from Monday's close of around 9,740/85. \par \par \uc2  "We saw large buyings from banks going long on dollars and some importers in the morning," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "The BNR moved to cap the downswing otherwise I think the leu might have weakened to about the 10,000 level." \par \par \uc2  The leu firmed to about 9,780/800 following the BNR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but some dealers said the unit would remain under pressure with the BNR likely to show up on the market again during Tuesday's trading. \par \par \uc2  Last week the BNR had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market selling moderate amounts of dollars to ease pressure on the leu which depreciated around four percent over the past month. ((Radu Marinas, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 312-0264, fax +40 1 315-8448, bucharest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dub305hhf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
