\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early, Seen Depreciating \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1998\par 09:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Friday, with dealers saying pressure on the leu is increasing. \par \par \uc2  At 0650 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,610 and ROL9,630, from between ROL9,585 and ROL9,595 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu depreciated early in the session on the increasing dollar demand from banks. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the pressure on the leu also is the result of fears of a further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The decrease of money market rates also pushed the banks to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and dollars. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market and selling dollars in a stormy session Thursday to stop the leu depreciation. Dealers said the bank sold a little less than $10 million. \par \par \uc2  The leu's depreciation Thursday also was caused by a high dollar demand for energy imports. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again Friday to control the leu's fall. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate dropped to 85% early in the session Friday from 125% Thursday, after banks met their reserve requirements. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated earlier that the leu will depreciate by 3% per month by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-10-98 \