\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Steady Vs Dlr In Calm Early Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1998\par 09:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is steady against the dollar early Friday, with dealers predicting little movement during the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0635 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,430 and ROL9,445, the same as Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu's level is likely to steady around the current value for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  He predicted the unit would continue its slow depreciation next week, amid low rates on the money market which makes banks interested in dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, a signal that the slow depreciation of the leu was expected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Two weeks ago the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly when the leu's depreciation accelerated, selling around $30 million. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate increased to 55% early in the session Friday, from 45% Thursday, with dealers predicting the rates will go up next week. \par \par \uc2  The leu is expected to continue its downward trend of 3% a month against the dollar until the end of the year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0723GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duan00ete\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
