\par\par \b \uc2  Romania Leu Lower Vs Dlr Early; Seen Stabilizing \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1998\par 08:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST (Dow Jones)--The Romanian leu (ROL) is lower against the dollar early Thursday, but a further decline during the session is seen as unlikely, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0635 GMT, the dollar was trading between ROL9,425 and ROL9,445, up from between ROL9,405 and ROL9,415 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said the leu's falls against the dollar early in the session was the result of just a few trades, adding that he expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady around current levels. \par \par \uc2  He also said he sees only a slight decline in the leu ahead of the weekend, with the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell dollars to halt any major falls. \par \par \uc2  The overnight money market rate dropped to 45% early in the session Thursday, from 55% Wednesday and 115% Tuesday. Dealers said the drop came as some of the deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weren't renewed, lifting leu liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predict money market rates will rise again in coming days, as banks have to meet end-month minimum reserve requirements. \par \par \uc2  The leu is expected to continue its downward trend in coming weeks, falling by 3% a month against the dollar until the end of the year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Cristi Cretzan; (401) 210-8197; ccretzan@\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 .ro \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0657GMT \par \par \uc2  1869 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duam00clw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\sh